cent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\nThe Client-side redirect loop detection always triggers on the second redirect.\r\nServer-side seems to be working.\r\n\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nCreate three routes:\r\n* `/` with a link to `/a`\r\n* `/a` with `export const load = () => ({ status: 302, redirect: '/b' });`\r\n* `/b` with `export const load = () => ({ status: 302, redirect: '/' });`\r\n\r\nWhen you click on the link to `/a`, a \"Redirect loop\" error will be shown.\r\n\r\nThis happens because `this.current.page.path` is pushed into the `chain` array here: https://github.com/sveltejs/kit/blob/7e51473ba715ecfe01238e051cc5c5224fcee0a6/packages/kit/src/runtime/client/renderer.js#L201-L204\r\nIn the next iteration, `chain.includes(this.current.page.path)` always is true here: https://github.com/sveltejs/kit/blob/7e51473ba715ecfe01238e051cc5c5224fcee0a6/packages/kit/src/runtime/client/renderer.js#L195\r\n\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nIt should be possible to do more then one redirect.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Severity**\r\nlow\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Rich-Harris","id":1162160,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjIxNjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1162160?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris","html_url":"https://github.com/Rich-Harris","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rich-Harris/events{/privacy}","received_ev